  "notes": "USAGE:\nImplies strong, authoritative leadership that brings people together under a common direction. More formal and powerful than {指導|しどう}する (to guide/instruct).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {統率力|とうそつりょく} (leadership ability)\n- {統率|とうそつ}のとれた (well-organized, unified)\n- {軍|ぐん}を{統率|とうそつ}する (to command an army)\n- チームを{統率|とうそつ}する (to lead a team)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {指揮|しき}する: to command — often used for military or musical direction\n- {率|ひき}いる: to lead — more literary, used for leading troops or groups",
